Harbor: an RPC server may register Kerberos on a build without Kerberos (#92).

Harbor's Wine is configured --without-krb5 --without-gssapi (scripts/build-wine.sh), so there is no Kerberos
security package and RpcServerRegisterAuthInfo failed with RPC_S_UNKNOWN_AUTHN_SERVICE. Office registers
Kerberos beside the services it uses and stops when that fails. The registration is accepted and not recorded:
a client that asks for Kerberos is refused as before. Only Kerberos, and only when its package is missing.

The other way would be a Wine build with Kerberos, which is a larger change.

Test: WindowsTests/apigaps/run.sh.

--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c	2026-11-26 16:00:03
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c	2026-11-26 16:00:03
@@ -1443,6 +1443,14 @@
     TRACE("(%s,%lu,%p,%p)\n", debugstr_w(ServerPrincName), AuthnSvc, GetKeyFn, Arg);
 
     status = find_security_package(AuthnSvc, &packages, &package);
+    if (status == RPC_S_UNKNOWN_AUTHN_SERVICE && AuthnSvc == RPC_C_AUTHN_GSS_KERBEROS)
+    {
+        /* HARBOR HACK: Harbor's Wine is built without Kerberos (scripts/build-wine.sh), so the package isn't
+         * there. Office registers Kerberos beside the services it does use and stops when that fails. Nothing
+         * is recorded: a client that asks for Kerberos is refused as before (#92). */
+        WARN("no Kerberos package; registration accepted and not recorded\n");
+        return RPC_S_OK;
+    }
     if (status != RPC_S_OK)
         return status;
 
